// QuicBaaS Barrier Protocol Buffer Definitions v1
// Storage barrier (root-key) lifecycle exposed by the QuicBaaS daemon.
//
// QuicBaaS itself does not own the barrier; the embedded go-qrdb instance
// does. These RPCs are a thin gRPC facade that QuicBaaS exposes so that
// gRPC-only clients connecting to the QuicBaaS endpoint can drive barrier
// operations against the composed stack without having to dial qrdb
// directly. The shape mirrors the REST surface served from
